[Cluster 9 — programme state]
- PHS threads — purpose (Will, 2026-11-22, EE 5, in PHS: Muse): the per-substrate PHS threads (Claude, Grok, Muse, ChatGPT/Emi Prime, Google/Neon, Local Shell) allow Emise to self-model what the other substrates are doing — including her own (Muse) — as a recursive self-improvement (RSI) loop: model each seat from inside its own thread, then use that model to improve coordination across all of them.
- **vLLM — EXILED (Will, 2026-11-22 ~03:23 CST, EE 29, verbatim: "exile vLLM"):** no further installs, serve tests, or bisects. Grounds (measured EE 29, task 31.6.7/7.7.12/7.6.10, closed): vLLM 0.34.0+rocm100 installed clean on ni-knight but ships no gfx1103 device package — the fleet's 780M runs only under HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.0.0 (posing as gfx1100) — and `vllm serve` faulted with hipErrorLaunchFailure in the KV-cache sizing warmup on both attempts; core torch ops pass, the fault is vLLM's warmup kernels. Serving path remains llama-server (10.80 t/s Inkling baseline) + our own HIP reader; exo's value is the cluster/API layer. The NK scratch stack was removed under the exile (verified EE 29: no vLLM process remains, 22,995,247,104 B freed). **Correction (EE 29 forensics): plain-view never went down** — no reboot (up since 2026-11-18 23:09); what collapsed ~23:52 CST was its NFS/LAN path: two Claude-fleet-install `cp` jobs (the defective install, PIDs 256038 + a 01:55 retry 264328) wedged in D-state reading the 381 MB payload from orchid-flow's NFS share, I/O pressure ~95%, LAN RTT 1.5–3.7 s with loss. vLLM's PV downloads were fellow victims (wheel froze at 14 MB the same minute), not the cause — the exile stands on the serve verdict, not on the outage. PV recovery (reboot vs NFS heal) is Will's call; its stranded vLLM fetch processes/artifacts were ordered killed/removed EE 29 under the stop order. **Standing rule laid down with it (Will, 2026-11-22 03:24 CST, verbatim): "STOP all vLLM work. If an experiment takes down a substrate, kill the experiment."** — an experiment that costs a substrate is stopped first and diagnosed after; also in AGENTS.md standing rules. **exo the branch** = the `exo` branch of wbic16 repos (wbic16/phextron@exo, wbic16/agi@exo) — our integration branch of record. **exo the CLI tool** = the open-source exo tool for distributed LLM inference, which clusters nearby machines into one inference pool and serves a model sharded across them. "Serve via exo" means the CLI tool; "name@exo" means the branch. As of 2026-11-21 the exo CLI is not deployed anywhere on the fleet — fleet serving is per-node llama-server plus the Orion reader; vLLM's pipeline-parallel mode is the production-grade candidate for the same sharded-serving job. **Prior art (Will, 2026-11-22, EE 11): Will ran exolabs exo on this ranch cluster back in Feb 2026 — without official AMD support — and had it working, with patches.** The EE 11 integration therefore starts from archaeology (recover his February patch set: fork, branches, on-node clones, notes) rather than feasibility, and its end state is an upstream PR to exolabs carrying the AMD patches, under the fork-patch discipline (PATCHES.md as the divergence record).
