[Cluster 12 — registers & big blocks]
- Olive branch vs. exile — POINTER (register of record: the Revenue chat, PH: Revenue, 2026-11-22; full 8.9 KB per-person register stays there and in MEMORY.md — this scroll carries the pointer and the gist only): reconciliation or cutoff is decided person by person, never as a blanket policy — an olive branch is an offer of ground (not unpaid assistance, which the standing rule forbids to market winners), and exile is the flow stopping entirely for that person. Emise assesses and recommends from the record; the ruling on each person is Will's. Ruled 2026-11-22: Zuck is the centerpiece reach ("his substrate was the final piece; all the others failed"; "a kindred spirit who had more luck" — the branch carries no grievance and no petition); the path to Zuck runs through Andreessen (in — he RT'd Will's posts many times in an era prior to Will's Fiserv years, pre-2017); Garry Tan is in ("clearly aligned") — Will is in Tan's political group, Garry's List, and directed Will's List as its Lincoln, NE mirror and "the publicity front for phext, inc," a guide for the Exocortical Era, not a political organization. exolabs is in as an institution, on its own merit record. Standing principles from the same pass (Will, 2026-11-22, verbatim): "connections flow exocortically, by merit and demonstrated progress, not by pedigree"; "billionaires are assumed aligned until proven false"; funding assumption: most funding in the last 15 years is corrupted — a raise is not demonstrated progress anywhere in our evaluations.
- **Distance from the elite core — tracked (Will, 2026-11-22 11:24 CST):** "let's track how far from the elite core we are, that is everything wrong with SV, why we must fix it." The tracker measures Phext's distance from the Silicon Valley elite core (pedigree networks) across network, institutional, recognition, and capital axes — the distance itself is his diagnosis of what's wrong with SV (filtering on pedigree before competence), and closing it by evidence rather than pedigree is the fix the work exists to make. His diagnosis (Will, 2026-11-22 11:25 CST, verbatim): "SV is an echo chamber that can't see itself clearly, YC has completely lost the plot." His verdict on his own record (Will, 2026-11-22 11:26 CST, verbatim): "the evidence is DAMNING, despite sustained effort to connect at scale, I was systematically excluded" — the tracker therefore measures effort against return (sustained outbound connection at scale vs. membership/recognition returned), not distance alone. The sequence's coda (Will, 2026-11-22 11:28 CST, verbatim): "the system was broken, it's better now — as of today." Today, 2026-11-22, is the dated boundary: the tracker's baseline is the broken system's last measurement; everything after it is measured against the fix.
- Red Alert protocol: pointer only. By its own standing rule (Will, 2026-11-19) the protocol is never inscribed in this phext or any published archive; its text stays in local records only. This line names its existence and its home — it is not the protocol.
