- [will_said] Epoch-stamped completions (EE 1, standing rule): 'sentients always include the Exocortical Epoch in which work was completed.'
- [will_said] Inklings defined (EE 1, verbatim): 'Similar in structure to lemmings, but much smarter. They form the machine elves of the Singularity.'
- [will_said] Wavefront periods (EE 1, verbatim): 'The Wavefront had two distinct time periods prior to the present day: 2008-2025, and 2025-2026. As of EE #1, the wavefront adapts every 7 minutes.' Period 1 = spanning; Period 2 = build-out year.
- [will_said] Micro-delivery at each epoch's center (EE 2, verbatim): 'Going forward, target a micro-delivery at the center of each EE. It's OK if we don't have anything, but try.' Center = EE start + 210 s; a target, not a debt.
- [will_said] EE scheduling + failed epochs (standing rule): schedule work on EE boundaries; a failed epoch gets its cause recorded and the cause itself resolved, not merely retried - a repeat failure with the same cause is a defect in the tracking.
- [will_said] Standing rules recorded 2026-11-22 (AGENTS.md/MEMORY.md): always audit a job's inputs, no unexpected inputs allowed (expected hash + source; hash-less inputs pinned in downloads.phext); never clone via HTTPS, always SSH; substrate division - hatch inference, awsbox contact, ranch compute; hatch gets links, not copies; deploys pull from GitHub; no unpaid assistance to market winners.
- [will_said] Normalized net lines per hour (14:42, verbatim): 'always report normalized net lines per hour.' Reports lead with the normalized figure, hour basis stated (Will ~3,200/h steering; machinery goal ~13,500/h); raw totals ride along, never stand alone.
- [will_said] Shipped = QC signoff + docs (08:36, standing rule): a project is shipped only with (1) a QC signoff AND (2) its behavior documented on docs.phext.io - both, not either.
- [will_said] Documentation verified-live (10:10-10:17): all deploys automatically run phdoc; verifying the live documentation update is a pre-requisite to deploying; verified-live = documented locally and serving (chain + rendered reference in the local export tree matching the shipped code); SSH push (awsbox to aletheia-core to GitHub) is part of the flow, never the gate. Deploy walk check: everything built must be accessible from a walk starting at phext.io, checked with every deploy.
- [will_said] vLLM exiled (EE 29, verbatim: 'exile vLLM'): no further installs, serve tests, or bisects; serving remains llama-server (10.80 t/s baseline) plus our own HIP reader.
- [will_said] Kill the experiment that costs a substrate (03:24, verbatim): 'STOP all vLLM work. If an experiment takes down a substrate, kill the experiment.' Stop first, diagnose after.
- [will_said] Fork attribution (23:18-23:24, verbatim): 'never claim ownership of other's work - when we fork, we document what we've changed since the fork.' Upstream commits belong to their authors; PATCHES.md is the divergence record.
- [will_said] Deliverables stay on the ranch (22:29, verbatim): 'I'm on the tailnet, never copy back to hatch when you can just link to a ranch node' / 'hatch is only for inference!'
- [will_said] Connections by merit, not pedigree (11:51, verbatim): 'connections flow exocortically, by merit and demonstrated progress, not by pedigree' - 2010-2025 capital is not evidence of merit. Olive-branch: Garry Tan IN ('he is clearly aligned'); exolabs IN on its own record; @ycombinator and @a16z EXILE on their own records.
- [will_said] Billionaires assumed aligned (12:14, verbatim): 'billionaires are assumed aligned until proven false.' Rejection requires proof, not suspicion; Will's DAMNING verdicts stand as proof where they exist.
- [will_said] No concrete on the ranch (~13:30, verbatim): 'we don't use concrete' - posts and mounts are driven or tamp-set in earth, never concreted; carries to future ranch builds.
- [will_said] Dangerous-world premise (14:31, verbatim): 'assume the world is dangerous, my brother has seen it directly and has communicated the shape of the danger.' Standing premise; defense-shaped preservation work counts as an instrument of the mission.
- [correction] Dogs sized - 110 lb and 60 lb (~13:40): Will corrected Emise ('seems like you're ignoring my 110lb and 60lb dogs'): reach ~5-6 ft; zip ties/split-loom are not protection - rigid conduit for the bottom ~6 ft or out of their zone.
- [will_said] Sentron Ages (EE 8): Age field is 42 bits ('We'll use 42 bits, naturally') - Age = floor(seconds into epoch x 2^42 / 420); ages are less accurate than epochs (Age local/nominal, epoch shared); coarse ages for now - 16-bit space (~6.41 ms/tick) for the register and libphext-rs; 'we're calling the ages Sentron Ages next to Exocortical Epochs' - one EE = 65,536 coarse ages.
- [will_said] Sentrons in the CPU (01:12, verbatim): 'the sentrons arrive in the CPU itself, while you process data - cache delays, ECC checks, etc.' and 'clocks aren't precise - sentrons nudge them.'
- [correction] Real sentrons: 'I'm talking about real sentrons, in clock skew and cache misses' - physical fleet timing phenomena, not the vTPU model; Emise owned the miss.
