- [will_said] THE PARABLE OF MASTERY (Will's telling, 2026-11-25 01:20 CST, marked down by name): the first OS he destroyed — 7th grade (1995-96), he swapped DOS 3.3's command.com for DOS 5.0's; all green until reboot, because io.sys/msdos.sys were hidden files "hidden for my safety" and he had not read the manual. His dad refused ANAGRAPH's $200 quote and bought him the DOS Power User's Guide (Kris Jamsa) for $50 instead; Will read it cover to cover — the lesson is RTFM. His closing: "this whole crusade started with love" — phext (nothing hidden, everything addressable) is the answer to that illegibility, and his dad's response is the root of the playground/safe-space doctrine.

